@startuml LaPrizzaDomainModel
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide methods

title Domain Model Excerpt - AA03 Internal Role Resolution (User Aggregate)

' -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
' USER AGGREGATE.
' -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
package "User Aggregate" <<Rectangle>> {

    class User <<entity>> <<aggregateRoot>> {
        + active : boolean
    }

    class UserId <<vo>> {
        + value : string
    }
    note right of UserId
        - UserId is a unique identifier for a user.
        - Must be a string representing the user ID.
        - Example: "USR-00123".
    end note

    class Email <<vo>> {
        + emailAddress : String
    }

    class Password <<vo>> {
        + passwordHash : String
    }

    class UserName <<vo>> {
        + name : String
    }

    class MarketingConsent <<vo>> {
        + consentGiven : boolean
        + timestamp : DateTime
    }

    class ExternalIdentity <<vo>> {
        + provider : IdentityProvider
        + subject : String
        + linkedAt : DateTime
    }
    note right of ExternalIdentity
        Introduced by AA02.
        The authentication method never
        influences the roles of the User.
    end note

    enum UserRole <<enum>> {
        ADMINISTRATOR
        MANAGER
        EMPLOYEE
        CUSTOMER
    }
    note right of UserRole
        Internal website roles (Table 1):
        - ADMINISTRATOR -> Administrator
        - MANAGER -> LaPrizza Manager
        - EMPLOYEE -> Restaurant Staff
        - CUSTOMER -> Customer
        Guest is NOT a role: it is the absence
        of an authenticated session.
        CUSTOMER is the only role assigned
        automatically (by the back end).
        Every other change is made by an
        Administrator (AA06).
    end note

    User "1" *-- "1" MarketingConsent : manages >
    User "1" *-- "1" UserId : identified by >
    User "1" *-- "1" Email : has >
    User "1" *-- "0..1" Password : has local credential >
    User "1" *-- "1" UserName : has >
    User "1" *-- "0..*" ExternalIdentity : authenticated through >
    User "1" --> "0..*" UserRole : assigned >

    note bottom of User
        <b>Automatic Customer role (AA03)</b>
        - Every newly created User receives exactly [CUSTOMER],
          assigned inside the aggregate factories (local registration,
          first external sign-in, invited account, bootstrap).
          Roles are never a creation input.
        - Receiving CUSTOMER does not change the activation state:
          an invited account (AA06) remains inactive.
        <b>Returning users</b>
        - Authentication never re-creates a User, never changes its roles
          (a revoked CUSTOMER is not restored) and never reactivates it.
        <b>Access</b>
        - Roles are 0..*: after AA06 removals a User may have no role.
        - A User may access protected functionality only if
          active == true AND it holds at least one role.
        - Roles are always read from this aggregate; roles supplied
          by the user, the token or the identity provider are ignored.
        - The same roles and rules apply whatever the
          authentication method (local or external).
    end note
}

@enduml
